<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Era of Silence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1934–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Era of Silence was the period of authoritarian rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> that began with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats">Konstantin Päts</a>'s self-coup of 12 March 1934, carried out with General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-laidoner">Johan Laidoner</a> to prevent the Vaps movement from winning power. Parliament was suspended, parties were banned and the press was censored. A new constitution of 1938 partly restored parliamentary life before the Soviet occupation of 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/era-of-silence.jpg" alt="Era of Silence" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: SKopp, PeepP and ‍others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Estonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
